00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:30.500
Well, and I think that they seem to be very aware of the idea, like, this economy-based game is going to be boring for kids.

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:39.820
And I think they did actually a really good job of presenting every element of this game in a way to up the kind of interest to it.

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:42.440
Where it's like, yeah, you have these alien characters.

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:48.080
And, like, instead of it just being like, yeah, your character has more money, your character is better at farming.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.620
It's like these alien characters with these quirky little descriptions.

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:57.620
And then instead of just selecting a plot of land, you've got this sort of, like, race where you've got to get to it.

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:01.880
And instead of just deciding, okay, this is going to be farmland.

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:03.900
I'm going to pay for what I need in farmland.

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:09.800
It's like, no, you've got to, like, walk into a little store, get a little robot mule, outfit him with what you want,

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:12.300
and then, like, walk him across the map over to the thing.

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:14.160
And then finally this auction thing.

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:25.680
Instead of it just being, like, I'm going to bid this much, it's like this little, all these characters on the screen kind of doing this dance where they have to meet at wherever the agreed upon price will end up being.

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:35.100
It's like, they did some, they definitely did good work at, like, trying to, trying to make this more interesting for kids.

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:38.100
And after the auction, you're shown the scores.

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:40.640
It shows you first place, second place, and so on.

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:44.220
